I was looking over some of the old YANIs listed at the YANI database
(http://student.bvsd.k12.co.us/~schoonov/yani/yani.cgi) and noticed
one that proposed having different "safety" words for different
alignments: i.e. Elbereth for lawfuls and other words for neutrals and
chaotics.
I thought this sounded like a good idea (after all, there's no reason
why one deity should help everyone.) The problem with that is that
Elbereth is an Elven goddess, but given that Elves are automatically
chaotic, there's no way they'd ever be able to engrave Elbereth. This
does not make much sense.

What might work a little better is to have different words for
different races, instead. Elves would engrave Elbereth (obviously),
Orcs could use Morgoth, Dwarves could use Aule (all three from Lord of
the Rings.) Not sure what humans and gnomes would engrave -- any
ideas?

The consequences would include:

- hostile members of your own race would not respect the word.
- hostile members of other races could (if they have the necessary
tools and intelligence) engrave the word for their own race, which
would then cause you to be repelled from their square.
- if you attempt to engrave the word for the wrong race, something
nasty could happen -- you get blasted, thrown off the square in a
random direction, maybe even a small chance of being turned into a
member of that race?
- one negative consequence would be that, since engraving long words
can take more time and have other bad effects (making daggers duller,
for example), elves would be at a disadvantage. Perhaps this could be
overcome by limiting the engraving time to a given number of turns for
all the "magic" words?

Any comments?

